T* (Section 03 30 00.) Tj
T* (Curing: keep cast-in-place concrete wet for 7 days when the daily low stays above 40 F.) Tj
T* (Weather limit: do not place concrete when the air temperature is below 40 F or above 95 F.) Tj
T* (Strength: do not load the slab until test cylinders reach 75 percent of the specified) Tj
T* (strength.) Tj
T* (Project: Cedarline Training Hall, a one-story practice hall. This section covers the slab) Tj
T* (and the grade beams only.) Tj
T* (Mix: the practice mix is called CH-4000. Design strength is 4000 psi at 28 days. Water added) Tj
T* (on site is not allowed.) Tj
T* (Joints: saw cut control joints the morning after placement, at the spacing on sheet S-101.) Tj
T* (Finish: light broom finish on walking surfaces. Do not add a shake-on hardener.) Tj
T* (Cylinders: cast one set of three cylinders for every 50 cubic yards, and one set on the last) Tj
T* (truck of the day.) Tj
T* (Hot weather: shade the forms and start curing the same day. The temperature cap above is the) Tj
T* (placement rule.) Tj
T* (Cold weather: if the forecast low is under the temperature floor above, wait. Do not use a) Tj
T* (different number.) Tj
T* (Repair: honeycombing deeper than 1 inch is written up as an issue. It is not patched in) Tj
T* (secret.) Tj
